BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|Feb 
 12 - AI\, ML and Computer Vision Meetup en Español|Online
DTSTART:20260212T110000
CATEGORIES:ai,backend,cloud,data,devops,frontend,mobile,security
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nJoin our virtual meetup to hear talks from experts on cutting-edge topics
  across AI\, ML\, and computer vision.\n\nFeb 12\, 2026\n9 - 11 AM Pacific
 \nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/ai-ml-and-
 computer-vision-meetup-en-espanol-february-12-2026)**\n\n**AI On-Device: P
 otencia + Privacidad**\n\nDescubre como puedes aprovechar los modelos de A
 I para ejecutarlos directamente en tu dispositivo\, ofreciendo velocidad\,
  autonomía y privacidad real: los datos nunca abandonan tu teléfono. En 
 esta charla veremos cómo funciona\, qué posibilidades abre y por qué ma
 rca un antes y un después en la relación entre usuario y tecnología.\n\
 n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Eury Pérez Beltré](https://www.linkedin.com/in/
 euryperez/) en Android con 14 años de experiencia en el sector. Ha trabaj
 ado con marcas como Under Armour\, BeachBody\, Citizen\, AdAction\, Mode M
 obile entre otros.\n\n**The magic of video generation! (Spanish)**\n\nVide
 o generation is no longer limited to cloud platforms like Google Veo3 and 
 others!\n\nYou can also do it with open-source software—no cost and no r
 estrictions!\nIn this talk\, you’ll discover the node-based interface Co
 mfyUI with models like Wan2.1. I’ll also give you a quick demo of an ope
 n-source extension I developed\, which has gained huge popularity in the c
 ommunity in just one month (1.2k stars on GitHub).\n\nAll of this LIVE!\n\
 n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Crystian Bietti](https://www.linkedin.com/in/crys
 tian/) apasionado por la tecnología en todos sus sabores.\nHoy: Maker esp
 ecializado con IA Generativa (Audiovisual + Agentes + Automatización + T
 écnico + Ponente + Divulgador)\nAyer: Arquitecto de software de aplicacio
 nes empresariales a gran escala.\n\n**Digital Twins: Building High-Fidelit
 y Virtual Worlds from Real-World Data**\n\nDigital twins provide a powerfu
 l framework for creating high-fidelity virtual representations of real env
 ironments\, enabling new forms of analysis\, interaction\, and decision-ma
 king. This talk will introduce the key principles behind building robust d
 igital twins from real-world data\, including capture workflows\, reconstr
 uction methods\, and scalability considerations. I will present several us
 e cases across domains such as cultural heritage\, industrial environments
  and operations\, virtual production\, and interactive or gamified applica
 tions\, illustrating how digital twins deliver measurable value in diverse
  contexts. The session will highlight how these models can integrate with 
 computational pipelines\, opening the door to applications that require hi
 gh realism and scientific reliability. This general overview will establis
 h a foundation that accommodates deeper exploration of specific applicatio
 ns during the live presentation.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Rubén Bernard
 ino](https://www.linkedin.com/in/ruben-bernardino/) is an industrial engin
 eer with nearly 30 years of international experience in engineering\, cult
 ural heritage\, and emerging media technologies. As the founder and Projec
 t Lead at Dronícola\, he develops high-fidelity digital twins and spatial
 -computing workflows that combine drones\, LiDAR\, photogrammetry\, artifi
 cial intelligence\, and game engines such as Unreal Engine for application
 s in virtual production\, immersive environments\, training\, and smart-in
 dustry operations. His background includes senior engineering roles at Gen
 eral Motors\, Ford\, and Fiat Chrysler\, complemented by studies in digita
 l innovation and XR technologies at Stanford\, Wageningen\, and Picterra U
 niversity.\n\n**A Practical Pipeline for Synthetic Data with Nano Banana P
 ro + FiftyOne**\n\nMost computer-vision failures come from the rare cases\
 , the dark corners\, odd combinations\, and edge conditions we never captu
 re enough in real datasets. In this session\, we walk through a practical 
 end-to-end pipeline for generating targeted synthetic data using Google’
 s Nano Banana Pro and managing it with FiftyOne. We’ll explore how to tr
 anslate dataset gaps into generation prompts\, create thousands of high-qu
 ality synthetic images\, automatically enrich them with metadata\, and bri
 ng everything into FiftyOne for inspection\, filtering\, and validation. B
 y the end\, you’ll understand how to build a repeatable synthetic-first 
 workflow that closes real vision gaps and improves model performance on th
 e scenarios that matter most.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Adonai Vera](http
 s://www.linkedin.com/in/adonai-vera/) \\- Machine Learning Engineer & DevR
 el at Voxel51\\. With over 7 years of experience building computer vision 
 and machine learning models using TensorFlow\, Docker\, and OpenCV\\. I st
 arted as a software developer\, moved into AI\, led teams\, and served as 
 CTO\\. Today\, I connect code and community to build open\, production\\-r
 eady AI\, making technology simple\, accessible\, and reliable\\.
LOCATION:Online
END:VEVENT
