BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|Feb 
 18 - Feedback-Driven Annotation Pipelines for End-to-End ML Workflows|Onli
 ne
DTSTART:20260218T120000
CATEGORIES:ai,data,frontend,web
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nIn this technical workshop\, we’ll show how to build a feedback-driven 
 annotation pipeline for perception models using **[FiftyOne](https://docs.
 voxel51.com/index.html)**. We’ll explore real model failures and data ga
 ps\, and turn them into focused annotation tasks that then route through a
  repeatable workflow for labeling and QA. The result is an end-to-end pipe
 line keeping annotators\, tools\, and models aligned and closing the loop 
 from annotation\, curation\, back to model training and evaluation.\n\n**T
 ime and Location**\n\nFeb 18\, 2026\n10 - 11 AM PST\nOnline. **[Register f
 or the Zoom!](https://link.voxel51.com/26-0218-annotation-meetup)**\n\n**W
 hat you'll learn**\n\n* **Techniques for labeling the data that matters th
 e most** for annotation time and cost savings\n* **Structure human-in-the-
 loop workflows** for finding and fixing model errors\, data gaps\, and tar
 geted relabeling instead of bulk labeling\n* **Combine auto-labeling and h
 uman review** in a single\, feedback-driven pipeline for perception models
 \n* **Use label schemas and metadata as “data contracts”** to enforce 
 consistency between annotators\, models\, and tools\, especially for multi
 modal data\n* **Detect and manage schema drift** and tie schema versions t
 o dataset and model versions for reproducibility\n* **QA and review steps*
 * that surface label issues early and tie changes back to model behavior\n
 * **An annotation architecture** that can accommodate new perception tasks
  and feedback signals without rebuilding your entire data stack
LOCATION:Online
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kong Mexico City|Shadow AI to Governed AI: The Chief AI Officer’
 s Playbook|Online
DTSTART:20260219T100000
CATEGORIES:ai,backend,security,web
DESCRIPTION:Kong/MEXICO-CITY\nAs enterprises rapidly adopt AI\, teams are 
 deploying models across multiple providers—often without oversight\, cre
 ating operational blind spots and compliance risks. This webinar addresses
  the urgent challenges of shadow AI and fragmented model management\, offe
 ring a clear roadmap to centralized control with Kong AI Gateway. We'll ex
 plore the risks of ungoverned AI deployment and demonstrate how a governed
  API surface streamlines orchestration\, security\, and compliance.Discove
 r how leading organizations have used Kong Konnect to centralize AI access
 \, control costs\, and improve developer experience—all without disrupti
 ng existing workflows.\n\n**What you’ll learn:**\n\n* Identify and quant
 ify hidden financial\, security\, and compliance risks in shadow AI\n* Map
  AI gateway capabilities—authentication\, policy enforcement\, rate limi
 ting\, routing\, and audit logging—to your most urgent operational chall
 enges\n* Implement a phased migration from direct model calls to gateway-f
 irst architecture for rapid\, low-risk wins\n* Align platform\, security\,
  and compliance teams with a unified approach to AI governance\n* Enhance 
 developer experience while achieving end-to-end oversight and control
LOCATION:Online
END:VEVENT
